From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:42:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] adb: read a host's key no further than its packet

A host sends its public key (A_AUTH, ADB_AUTH_RSAPUBLICKEY) before it
is let in. adbd read it with std::string(p->payload.data()):

- a packet with no payload has a null data(), and std::string throws:
  adbd aborts, so anyone at the other end of the cable can stop it;
- a key without its terminating NUL is read past the end of the
  payload, into the heap.

Read at most the payload, up to its first NUL.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 packages/modules/adb/adb.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/modules/adb/adb.cpp b/packages/modules/adb/adb.cpp
index 78bbfb6..38df2d9 100644
--- a/packages/modules/adb/adb.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/adb.cpp
@@ -456,7 +456,15 @@ void handle_packet(apacket *p, atransport *t)
             }
 
             case ADB_AUTH_RSAPUBLICKEY:
-                t->auth_key = std::string(p->payload.data());
+                // The host sends its key as a C string, but nothing makes it
+                // end the payload with the NUL, or send a payload at all
+                // (then data() is null): read no further than the payload.
+                if (p->payload.empty()) {
+                    t->auth_key.clear();
+                } else {
+                    t->auth_key.assign(p->payload.data(),
+                                       strnlen(p->payload.data(), p->payload.size()));
+                }
                 adbd_auth_confirm_key(t);
                 break;
 #endif
